    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "Note that, in the proof of Lemma 12, we constructed very speciﬁc K-fat (K3,K1,3)-minors. In our K-fat K3-minor, the connected subgraphs H1,H2,H3 are disks. In our K-fat K1,3minor, the connected subgraphs H1,H2,H3 are singletons and the paths Pi,0, i = 1,2,3, are shortest paths. Even more speciﬁc K-fat (K3,K1,3)-minors were obtained in [1]. It was shown that if a graph G contains no (≥ K)-subdivision of K3 as a geodesic subgraph and no (≥ 3K)subdivision of K1,3 as a 3-quasi-geodesic subgraph, then pb(G) ≤ 18K + 2 (see [1] for details and deﬁnitions)."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 12,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 102.0, 410.073, 391.822, 420.982 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "From Lemma 12, we immediately get the following corollary."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 13,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 85.08, 370.113, 526.898, 394.582 ],
    "font" : "CMTI10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "Corollary 7. If G has neither K-fat K3-minor nor K-fat K1,3-minor, then mci(G) ≤ 4K−1. In particular, mci(G) ≤ 4 · mﬁ(G) + 3."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 14,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 85.079, 317.193, 526.996, 355.222 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "Proof. The ﬁrst part of Corollary 7 follows from Lemma 12. For the second part, let mﬁ(G) = K −1. Then, G has neither K-fat K3-minor nor K-fat K1,3-minor. By the ﬁrst part, mci(G) ≤ 4K − 1 = 4(K − 1) + 3 = 4 · mﬁ(G) + 3. ⊔⊓"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 15,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 85.08, 264.873, 405.982, 302.182 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "Combining Lemma 11 and Corollary 7 with Theorem 4, we get. Theorem 5. For every graph G,"
